#[doc("""
What a run says when it did not get through what it planned.

A pool that runs out of kalku ends the run, and the wekufe it had not cast
are not measured. A report built from the ones it did cast carries a score
and a clean exit, so a CI job or an agent reads a finished run. Saying
where it stopped, and why, is the only honest answer.
""")]

#[doc("""
Why a run is not a measurement, when it stopped before casting everything:
how far it got and what the pool said. `None` when it got through its plan,
whatever the pool said on the way out, since nothing was left unmeasured.
""")]
pub fn stopped_short(failure: Option[String], cast: Int, planned: Int) : Option[String] =
  match failure {
    Some(why) -> if cast < planned {
      Some("the run stopped after #{cast} of #{planned} wekufe: #{why}")
    } else {
      None
    }
    None -> None
  }
